cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Verity: multi-detector deepfake examination pipeline"
message: "If you use Verity in academic work, please cite this entry together with the upstream detector papers relevant to your panel."
version: 0.4.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ADPer0705/verity"
url: "https://github.com/ADPer0705/verity"
keywords:
  - deepfake detection
  - media forensics
  - explainability
  - image forensics
  - video forensics
  - audio anti-spoofing
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Verity is a deterministic, explainable examination pipeline for suspected
  manipulated images, videos and audio. It characterises the media, selects
  only the detectors that can consume it, executes each detector in an
  isolated version-pinned environment, and preserves every per-detector
  verdict, reasoning and explainability artifact. Model-free forensic
  analyzers (metadata, compression, noise, temporal, audio) run alongside the
  detectors. Verity never collapses the panel into a single real/fake score.
authors:
  - name: "ADPer"
